  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rNotice under Article 12: Request for Waiver of Planning Application Requirement (Local List) under Article 2 of The Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) (Amendment) Order 2015,\r\rLocation Plan (1:500),\r\rAerial View of the Site,\r\rFloor Plans,\r\rHighway Safety Impact Form,\r\rLocation Plan (1:1250).\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Within three months of the date of this permission, 4 long stay cycle parking spaces to satisfy the permitted number of occupiers on site shall have been fully provided.\r\rThe dedicated cycle store providing 4 long stay parking spaces shall fulfil the following:\r\rSiting: Located in a secure, covered area within the building or in a dedicated cycle store.\rAccess: The cycles store shall be step free accessible with aisles at least 1.5 meters wide to allow easy manoeuvring. Access to reach the store shall involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door).\rSecurity: Located with natural surveillance and good lighting, the cycles store shall be secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob to provide greater security.\r\rCycle parking shall be retained on site thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "Within three months of the date of this permission, waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the permitted number of occupiers shall have been provided on site, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities are to be retained thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets.\r",
    "The HMO hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than four residents at any one time, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r \rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not compromise standards of accommodation and does not adversely affect the residential amenities of neighbouring properties.\r"
  ],
